WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:08.152
- Did you ever feel, like
when you were being bullied

00:00:08.152 --> 00:00:11.319
that you wanted to take your own life?

00:00:12.181 --> 00:00:13.014
- Yeah.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:15.305
- Sorry.

00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:16.138
- [Woman] Yeah.

00:00:16.138 --> 00:00:18.555
(soft music)

00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:24.260
- Virginia and I met in middle school.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.313
Our relationship was basically,

00:00:27.313 --> 00:00:30.238
she was someone that I picked on.

00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:32.540
I was a bully to Virginia.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.253
- So, my first encounter with
bullying, I guess with her,

00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:38.026
probably was around fifth grade.

00:00:38.026 --> 00:00:41.899
- I think I said nasty things
about how much she weighed.

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:43.951
- The kids I went to school with

00:00:43.951 --> 00:00:45.931
in elementary and middle school,

00:00:45.931 --> 00:00:47.515
we all lived in the same neighborhood.

00:00:47.515 --> 00:00:51.091
So, I wouldn't come
outside most of the time,

00:00:51.091 --> 00:00:55.249
because most of the kids
that kind of were mean to me

00:00:55.249 --> 00:00:56.729
lived in my neighborhood.

00:00:56.729 --> 00:00:59.872
I can't say that I really
had any friends back then.

00:00:59.872 --> 00:01:01.860
- I was a bit underweight.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.027
I had glasses.

00:01:04.971 --> 00:01:07.659
I went through seven
years of orthodontic work.

00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:10.723
I was picked on for that
and so I would project it

00:01:10.723 --> 00:01:13.223
onto her for being overweight.

00:01:19.897 --> 00:01:22.685
- I guess the main question
would just be, why now?

00:01:22.685 --> 00:01:26.062
- As selfish as it sounds,
I don't wanna feel guilty

00:01:26.062 --> 00:01:30.346
for something that my
childhood self was doing.

00:01:30.346 --> 00:01:33.720
(door opening)

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.553
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.133
(footsteps)

00:01:40.905 --> 00:01:42.568
- How are you?
- I'm good, how are you?

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:43.485
- I'm good.

00:01:44.423 --> 00:01:45.256
You look good.

00:01:45.256 --> 00:01:46.089
- Thank you.

00:01:46.089 --> 00:01:46.922
So do you.

00:01:46.922 --> 00:01:47.953
(they laugh)

00:01:47.953 --> 00:01:52.120
- What do you remember
about me from grade school?

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.912
- You always were so
bubbly, I remember that.

00:01:56.912 --> 00:01:57.745
I don't know.

00:01:57.745 --> 00:02:01.041
What do you remember about me?

00:02:01.041 --> 00:02:05.208
- I remember more of what I
said about you and I don't--

00:02:06.298 --> 00:02:10.560
- I know a lot of the, I guess, the words,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.238
the harsh words were
more about my appearance.

00:02:13.238 --> 00:02:16.691
- I remember I was picking
on you about your weight.

00:02:16.691 --> 00:02:19.503
- Nobody noticed the
shift, but my grandmother

00:02:19.503 --> 00:02:23.346
passed away when I was in middle school

00:02:23.346 --> 00:02:26.679
and she used to take medicine for cancer

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.044
and it made her gain a lot of weight

00:02:30.044 --> 00:02:34.211
because she wasn't really
worried about how big she was.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.725
I kind of stopped worrying
about how big I got.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:42.558
People just kept bothering me and I think

00:02:42.558 --> 00:02:45.352
the major question was just, why me?

00:02:45.352 --> 00:02:48.369
I felt like I was always very nice to you

00:02:48.369 --> 00:02:50.418
and very nice to everybody else

00:02:50.418 --> 00:02:52.674
so it just, it bothered
me 'cause it was just like

00:02:52.674 --> 00:02:55.674
what did I ever do to you all for me

00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:59.406
to even be subjected to that?

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:03.876
- I was underweight and
I was takin' medicine

00:03:03.876 --> 00:03:08.043
to be a healthy weight and so
I was projectin' that on you

00:03:09.558 --> 00:03:12.240
and I don't think that
I even had any problem

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.907
with the way you looked
or your weight at all.

00:03:14.907 --> 00:03:16.740
- Why didn't you stop?

00:03:17.766 --> 00:03:21.933
- I was being bullied and so
I knew it was wrong, you know?

00:03:23.686 --> 00:03:27.746
I didn't want that done to
me but yet, I turn around

00:03:27.746 --> 00:03:29.850
and was doing it to other people.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.273
- I had no idea you were
being bullied, either.

00:03:32.273 --> 00:03:35.138
- It's funny you thought that
I was very bubbly and friendly

00:03:35.138 --> 00:03:36.610
'cause I was wearing this like,

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:41.010
I wear it better now and
more honest about my feelings

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.190
but I was definitely wearing a facade.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.023
- Right.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.226
- I'd go home, cry about it,
come back and be all like,

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:47.464
ne ne ne ne ne ne ne.

00:03:47.464 --> 00:03:48.297
- [Virginia] Mm hm.

00:03:48.297 --> 00:03:50.034
- And then I'd pick on
people that I felt like

00:03:50.034 --> 00:03:52.238
weren't gonna pick back with me.

00:03:52.238 --> 00:03:53.071
- Right.

00:03:53.071 --> 00:03:56.092
It's not you, I mean it wasn't just you

00:03:56.092 --> 00:03:59.423
so I'm not gonna sit here
and give you all of that.

00:03:59.423 --> 00:04:04.385
- Did you ever feel, like
when you were being bullied

00:04:04.385 --> 00:04:07.552
that you wanted to take your own life?

00:04:09.158 --> 00:04:09.991
- Yeah.

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:13.500
- Sorry.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:14.333
- Yeah.

00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:16.666
It was definitely a thought.

00:04:20.165 --> 00:04:22.812
This is probably the first time
I've ever said it out loud.

00:04:22.812 --> 00:04:23.951
Well, probably the second
time I've ever said it

00:04:23.951 --> 00:04:25.508
out loud but, yeah.

00:04:25.508 --> 00:04:29.146
I can't say that I
hadn't thought about it.

00:04:29.146 --> 00:04:32.825
It's such a sad thing to think about.

00:04:32.825 --> 00:04:35.455
Wait, you said you thought about this too?

00:04:35.455 --> 00:04:36.441
- Yes.

00:04:36.441 --> 00:04:38.422
Just short answer, yes.

00:04:38.422 --> 00:04:42.402
- I was insecure for a
long time about my weight,

00:04:42.402 --> 00:04:45.985
about my appearance,
about the way I dress.

00:04:49.146 --> 00:04:53.202
It took a long time for
me to kind of like me.

00:04:53.202 --> 00:04:55.525
- The more I'm listening to
you, the more I feel like, yeah.

00:04:55.525 --> 00:04:57.335
We had a lot in common.

00:04:57.335 --> 00:04:59.476
- It'd take a lot for
me to really hate you.

00:04:59.476 --> 00:05:01.475
I didn't feel like I hated you then.

00:05:01.475 --> 00:05:04.078
I don't feel like I hate you now.

00:05:04.078 --> 00:05:06.721
And it took a long time for me to say,

00:05:06.721 --> 00:05:09.909
even though I haven't said it to you,

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:12.150
that I forgive you as for that.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.396
It was a lot to deal with--
- I'm sorry.

00:05:14.396 --> 00:05:15.229
- It's okay.

00:05:15.229 --> 00:05:17.313
It was a lot to deal
with and I just wanted

00:05:17.313 --> 00:05:18.911
to move on from it.

00:05:18.911 --> 00:05:21.471
I've never actually
had something like that

00:05:21.471 --> 00:05:22.727
happen to me before.

00:05:22.727 --> 00:05:25.228
- I definitely did not
expect for Virginia and I

00:05:25.228 --> 00:05:26.934
to have so much in common.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:30.117
- It felt good, just to kinda close

00:05:30.117 --> 00:05:33.517
a sorta chapter in my life
that was pretty sucky.

00:05:33.517 --> 00:05:35.134
I know, it's okay!

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.928
- Even if you didn't let
me, I was gonna hug you.

00:05:36.928 --> 00:05:38.012
- Oh my God, no.

00:05:38.012 --> 00:05:39.640
- Yes.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:40.473
Yes.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:41.306
- You're like, I was gonna hug you anyway,

00:05:41.306 --> 00:05:42.762
'cause I don't care.

00:05:42.762 --> 00:05:45.762
(soft violin music)

